wg-quick (FreeBSD): keep the routes when the route monitor dies while the
interface is still up, and parse netstat's Netif column correctly.

- monitor_daemon's trap ran del_routes on any exit of the background
  monitor. Started from a script that then ends (cloud-init), the monitor
  is killed and deleted every route through the WireGuard interface.
  Now it only cleans up once the interface is gone.
- del_routes read Netif from field 6 of "netstat -nr -f inet"; it is
  field 4, so IPv4 routes were never matched (and the trap above only
  removed the IPv6 ones).

diff --git net/wireguard-tools/Makefile net/wireguard-tools/Makefile
index 708a203c3579..551b9b829031 100644
--- net/wireguard-tools/Makefile
+++ net/wireguard-tools/Makefile
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 PORTNAME=	wireguard-tools
 DISTVERSION=	1.0.20260223
-PORTREVISION=	2
+PORTREVISION=	3
 CATEGORIES=	net net-vpn
 MASTER_SITES=	https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-tools/snapshot/
 
diff --git net/wireguard-tools/files/patch-wg-quick_freebsd.bash net/wireguard-tools/files/patch-wg-quick_freebsd.bash
